  "previews": [
   "raw/medgfx/preview_medtitle_wall.png",
   "raw/medgfx/preview_medtitle_grey.png"
  ],
  "note": "Lettering on transparent for the dark blue-green wall, RGB plane uniformly warm cream #E9DFC6, left aligned, 44 px margins. Intro: 98 Chinese characters incl. punctuation (88 Han, 3 lines), 68 English words (5 lines); then the plain note that works, makers and dates are fictional; footer 展厅 2 · Gallery 2.",
  "colour": "#E9DFC6",
  "ink_box_px": [
   44,
   44,
   1056,
   956
  ],
  "text_zh": "金地不是背景，而是光本身。十三至十五世纪的画师在木板上敷石膏底、贴金箔，再以蛋彩层层细笔描绘。这些画为烛光与祈祷而作：火苗摇曳，压印的光环与金地随之明灭。请先退后看整体，再走近看笔触与金上的纹样。",
  "text_en": "A gold ground is not a background; it is light itself. Between about 1200 and 1450 painters laid gold leaf over gesso on wooden panels and built up figures in fine strokes of egg tempera. These pictures were made for candle-light and prayer, where tooled haloes flickered with the flame. Stand back for the whole, then come close for the brushwork and the patterns punched in the gold.",
  "note_zh": "本展厅的作品均为专为这个三维场景创作的图像，作者与年代为虚构。",
  "note_en": "The works in this room are images made for this 3D scene; makers and dates are fictional."
 },
